   "text": {
    "L1": "To multiply decimals, estimate first so the answer makes sense.",
    "L2": "A common mistake is saying 0.3 times 0.2 equals 0.6. That is not true.",
    "L3": "For 2.4 times 1.3, estimate about 2 times 1.5, which is about 3.",
    "L4": "Ignore the points first: 24 times 13 equals 312.",
    "L5": "There is one decimal place in each factor, so the product has two decimal places: 3.12.",
    "L6": "Tenths times tenths gives hundredths: 0.3 times 0.2 is 0.06, not 0.6.",
    "L7": "Now use the same idea: choose the product of 0.4 and 0.2."
   },
